-"","clip_id","newspaper_name","fulldate","p_number","secondary_p_number","url","text","narrative_detail","headline","num_turtles","species","spp_id","location_certainty","weight_lb","length_ft_inches","habitat","notes","year","data_quality_index","data_quality_cat","num_turtles_numeric","weight_kg","length_cm","decade","location","county_muni","state","country","latitude","longitude"
-"1","sdunion_19170402","""San Diego Union and Daily Bee""",1917-04-02,5,"na","""https://cdnc.ucr.edu/?a=d&d=SDDU19170402.2.68&srpos=32&e=-------en--20-SDDU-21--txt-txIN-turtle+NOT+florida+NOT+jersey+NOT+automobile-------""","“New Waters Near La Paz Promise Prolific Supply of Sea Food. \n Competition In the Lower California fisheries trade, advocated by the California state game and fish commission as a means of crating a supply greater than the demand, and therefore resulting in the lowering of the high cost of living, is beginning to bear fruit. \n For years fishermen operating out of this port have been compelled to pay tribute to certain concessional holders of fishing rights along the southern littoral for the privilege of operating in those waters. \n Independent fishermen, headed by M. Kondo, have now started fishing in waters south of the twenty eighth parallel under permits granted by the governor of La Paz. These waters form a prolific source of supply of halibut, barracuda, lobsters and other kinds of shellfish. \n Two California inspectors have been commissioned to go south with the lobster craft operating under permits issued by the governor of La Paz. These officers are being paid by the importers, as required by law. Their duties are to certify that the provisions of the California law governing lobster importation are respected. A third inspector will arrive here April 10. \n In addition to granting permits overriding the concessionaires operating for the Cantu government, the Mexican de facto government as represented in the La Paz regime has taken the California fish and game laws for its guidance in conserving the west Mexican fisheries and has appointed its own inspectors to accompany the boats to which it has issued permits, to see that the fishing craft take no young fish, use no trawl nets or other gear destructive of the future supply. \n Work of the concessionaires under this new competitive arrangement, fostered by the simplifying of importation under rulings of the fish and game commission, will extend to the fresh fish trade within a short time. Owing to the distance traveled refrigerating apparatus will have to be installed on boats operating to the new fishing grounds in the vicinity of Turtle and Magdalena bays. \n The auxiliary schooners None Such and Telemaches are now operating exclusively between this port and Turtle bay in the lobster and turtle carrying trade. Turtle meat now is being sold at 8 cents a pound In the California markets, and the demand is said to be far greater than the supply. \n Captain Robert Israel, who, with Kondo, is establishing an independent lobster and turtle trade at this port, and who is operating the None Such and Telemaches, plans to put another vessel in service between here and Turtle bay within a few weeks. \n The floating cannery John A. Heston is operating at Magdalena bay, engaged in the canning of turtle soup, sardines and other fish products. The Heston, during the tuna season, is expected to pack thousands of cases of this delectable sea food for shipment to San Diego, thence to be distributed to the Southern California, Western and Eastern markets. \n Five thousand pounds of halibut and barracuda arrived in port yesterday from the halibut banks north of Cedros on the fishing schooner Josephine Z.”","2","""PUBLIC TO BENEFIT FROM OPENING OF FISHING GROUNDS""","cargo","green","inferred","inferred",NA,NA,"not_reported","""location is not specified to an individual fishing site, but instead clarifies that fishing is 'south of the 28th parallel' and includes Magdalena bay, turtle bay, and La Paz""","1917",6,"medium",57.46875,NA,NA,1910,"turtle_bay","mulege","baja_california_sur","mexico",27.6943941,-114.8965209
-"2","sppilot_19171210","""San Pedro News Pilot""",1917-12-10,1,"na","""https://cdnc.ucr.edu/?a=d&d=SPNP19171210.2.11&srpos=15&e=-------en--20-SPNP-1--txt-txIN-turtle+NOT+story+NOT+florida+NOT+jersey+NOT+bangor+NOT+cuba+NOT+jamaica+NOT+chicago+NOT+snapping+NOT+turn+NOT+turned+NOT+turns+NOT+turning+NOT+deck+NOT+dove+NOT+doves+NOT+house+NOT+pond+NOT+lake+NOT+York+NOT+desert+NOT+race+NOT+school+NOT+neck+NOT+mock+NOT+necks-------""","""W. W. Beach, of 437 North Mesa street, has been experimenting for some years in canning various kinds of crustaceans and other sea animal life, and has now hit upon what he thinks will be one of the most highly priced delicacies every placed on the market. The product is called “turtle stock,” and consists of Calipash, Calipee and other edible parts of the green turtle, put up In a concentrated form for the making of turtle soup. \n Enormous numbers of these green turtles have been brought up from Magdalena and Turtle bays for years past and sold alive in the Los Angeles and San Francisco markets. This is probably the first successful method of canning the turtle so that it can be placed on the market in a practicable and preserved form. \n The formula states that the soup should contain besides the one pound can of turtle stock, one pound of carrots, one pound of ham, 1/2 pound of veal, 1/2 pound of onions, 2 eggs, hard-boiled, 1/2 lemon, 2 pounds of tomatoes, strained, 1 large glass of port, sherry or maideria wine, 1 large tablespoonful of beef drippings, 1 tablespoonful of Cury. This will make one gallon of the most delicious turtle soup, enough for sixteen people, which will keep for several days, if reheated once in forty-eight hours. \n Mr. Beach has arranged to have the turtles brought here in local boats and the product will be put up by the White Star Canning Co., at East San Pedro. It is thought that the possibilities of the industry are large and that one more form of food has been wrested from the mysteries of the great Pacific ocean, lying practically unexplored and teeming with many forms of life which may yet go far toward solving the problem of supplying the ever increasing demand for something new in food stuffs.""","2","""WILL PACK TURTLES AT WHITE STAR""","cargo","green","reported","known",NA,NA,"not_reported","""This is connected to sppilot_19190319. This is not a reporting of a specific cargo shipment/capture, nor is it for one particular time. It merely claims that there were consistent shipments of these turtles over the years to fuel the canning industry. Additionally, it cites both magdalena and turtle bays as locations, hence the two labels for location""","1917",8,"high",57.46875,NA,NA,1910,"turtle_bay","mulege","baja_california_sur","mexico",27.6943941,-114.8965209
