-"6","stinson_sdherald_18710615","""San Diego Herald""",1871-06-15,NA,"51","""https://georgehbalazs.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Stinson_1984_BiologyofSeaTurtlesSanDiegoBayCAinNEPacOcean_Thesis_SDSU.pdf""","""A firm in this city is in receipt of a letter from a large house in San Francisco making inquiries in relation to the possibility of receiving a steady supply of turtle through this port. The San Diego firm has replied offering to contract to supply any stated quantity, from one up to ten thousand pounds, by each steamer, or even more if desired. Turtles are found in abundance at Turtle Bay... or at Scammon's Lagoon... and can be supplied to the San Francisco dealers very cheaply.""","1","""Historic and Economic Importance of Sea Turtles to San Diego""","cargo","green","inferred","known",NA,NA,"not_reported","""no precise number given, just says that they are found 'in abundance', and seemingly enough to support a fishery/industry.""","1871",6,"medium",57.46875,NA,NA,1870,"scammons_lagoon","mulege","baja_california_sur","mexico",27.7499996,-114.25
-"7","stinson_sdherald_18710615","""San Diego Herald""",1871-06-15,NA,"51","""https://georgehbalazs.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Stinson_1984_BiologyofSeaTurtlesSanDiegoBayCAinNEPacOcean_Thesis_SDSU.pdf""","""A firm in this city is in receipt of a letter from a large house in San Francisco making inquiries in relation to the possibility of receiving a steady supply of turtle through this port. The San Diego firm has replied offering to contract to supply any stated quantity, from one up to ten thousand pounds, by each steamer, or even more if desired. Turtles are found in abundance at Turtle Bay... or at Scammon's Lagoon... and can be supplied to the San Francisco dealers very cheaply.""","1","""Historic and Economic Importance of Sea Turtles to San Diego""","cargo","green","inferred","known",NA,NA,"not_reported","""no precise number given, just says that they are found 'in abundance', and seemingly enough to support a fishery/industry.""","1871",6,"medium",57.46875,NA,NA,1870,"turtle_bay","mulege","baja_california_sur","mexico",27.6943941,-114.8965209
-"8","stinson_sdherald_18870326","""San Diego Herald""",1887-03-26,NA,"54","""https://georgehbalazs.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Stinson_1984_BiologyofSeaTurtlesSanDiegoBayCAinNEPacOcean_Thesis_SDSU.pdf""","""It is a singular fact that turtle is appreciated in California neither as an article of food nor an element of commerce. Californians can hardly be persuaded to eat turtle. In New York, and the East generally, and over the whole world, turtle is regarded as a great delicacy. [Captain Bogart] informed me that turtle exist in wonderful quantities on the Lower California coast. It may be impossible to make a market for the dainty in California, but the meat can be packed and exported. Captain Bogart informs us that Scammon’s Lagoon, several lagoons to the north of it, and the bay at Cerros [Cedros] Island are crammed with turtle. Many sloughs open into the lagoons, and the practice of the turtle is to float up them at flood-tide and feed. Captain Bogart, by stretching a seine over the mouth of these sloughs, has captured eight tons at a single haul. He could have taken more but had no room for them.”","1","""Historic and Economic Importance of Sea Turtles to San Diego""","cargo","green","inferred","known",NA,NA,"not_reported","na","1887",6,"medium",57.46875,NA,NA,1880,"cedros_island","ensenada","baja_california","mexico",28.2012034,-115.2522841
