+"1","sppilot_19171210","""San Pedro News Pilot""",1917-12-10,1,NA,"""https://cdnc.ucr.edu/?a=d&d=SPNP19171210.2.11&srpos=15&e=-------en--20-SPNP-1--txt-txIN-turtle+NOT+story+NOT+florida+NOT+jersey+NOT+bangor+NOT+cuba+NOT+jamaica+NOT+chicago+NOT+snapping+NOT+turn+NOT+turned+NOT+turns+NOT+turning+NOT+deck+NOT+dove+NOT+doves+NOT+house+NOT+pond+NOT+lake+NOT+York+NOT+desert+NOT+race+NOT+school+NOT+neck+NOT+mock+NOT+necks-------""","""W. W. Beach, of 437 North Mesa street, has been experimenting for some years in canning various kinds of crustaceans and other sea animal life, and has now hit upon what he thinks will be one of the most highly priced delicacies every placed on the market. The product is called “turtle stock,” and consists of Calipash, Calipee and other edible parts of the green turtle, put up In a concentrated form for the making of turtle soup. \n Enormous numbers of these green turtles have been brought up from Magdalena and Turtle bays for years past and sold alive in the Los Angeles and San Francisco markets. This is probably the first successful method of canning the turtle so that it can be placed on the market in a practicable and preserved form. \n The formula states that the soup should contain besides the one pound can of turtle stock, one pound of carrots, one pound of ham, 1/2 pound of veal, 1/2 pound of onions, 2 eggs, hard-boiled, 1/2 lemon, 2 pounds of tomatoes, strained, 1 large glass of port, sherry or maideria wine, 1 large tablespoonful of beef drippings, 1 tablespoonful of Cury. This will make one gallon of the most delicious turtle soup, enough for sixteen people, which will keep for several days, if reheated once in forty-eight hours. \n Mr. Beach has arranged to have the turtles brought here in local boats and the product will be put up by the White Star Canning Co., at East San Pedro. It is thought that the possibilities of the industry are large and that one more form of food has been wrested from the mysteries of the great Pacific ocean, lying practically unexplored and teeming with many forms of life which may yet go far toward solving the problem of supplying the ever increasing demand for something new in food stuffs.""","2","""WILL PACK TURTLES AT WHITE STAR""","cargo","green","reported","known","not_reported","not_reported","not_reported","""This is connected to sppilot_19190319. This is not a reporting of a specific cargo shipment/capture, nor is it for one particular time. It merely claims that there were consistent shipments of these turtles over the years to fuel the canning industry. Additionally, it cites both magdalena and turtle bays as locations, hence the two labels for location""","1917",8,"high",NA,57.46875,NA,1910,"turtle_bay","mulege","baja_california_sur","mexico",27.6943941,-114.8965209
