 "7","cejournal_19170331","""Coronado Eagle and Journal""",1917-03-31,1,NA,"""https://cdnc.ucr.edu/?a=d&d=CJ19170331.2.4&srpos=21&e=--1846---1973--en--20-CJ-21--txt-txIN-turtle+NOT+story+NOT+florida+NOT+jersey+NOT+bangor+NOT+cuba+NOT+jamaica+NOT+chicago+NOT+snapping+NOT+turn+NOT+turned+NOT+turns+NOT+turning+NOT+deck+NOT+dove+NOT+doves+NOT+house+NOT+pond+NOT+lake+NOT+York+NOT+desert+NOT+race+NOT+school+NOT+neck+NOT+mock+NOT+necks-------""","""Live turtles and lobsters were plentiful around the municipal pier Wednesday morning when two boats arrived from Turtle bay on the Lower California coast. \n The auxiliary schooner Nonesuch brought its first load from the camps recently established by the Israel brothers, the delivery being 21 turtles and 58 crates of lobsters. The Telemachus, Captain Olson, brought 20 turtles and 49 crates of lobsters. \n Turtle steaks and soup will be on the menu at del Coronado for a day or two, as five big turtles were brought over for the delectation of the palates of guests. One of the turtles weighed 275 pounds, and the other four were almost as large, except a little one that Manager Hernan may decide to use as a mascot. Turtles cost 6c a pound as they come from the water, and there is lots of bone in their shell.""
