-"51","stinson_sdunion_19030524","""San Diego Union and Daily Bee""",1903-05-24,NA,"48","""https://georgehbalazs.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Stinson_1984_BiologyofSeaTurtlesSanDiegoBayCAinNEPacOcean_Thesis_SDSU.pdf""","""Peter Stanovitch brought in fourteen large turtles which he had caught during the night, the largest one weighing 500 pounds [230 kg]. The turtles were captured in the shallow waters of the mud flats where they breed at this time of the year.""","2","""History of Sea Turtles in San Diego Bay""","14","green","inferred","san_diego","inferred","500","not_reported","""mud flats""","""fishermen supposedly believed that these turtles were the children of the children of the turtles from baja california that escaped from their corral in the san diego bay in 1857, but evidence is unclear""","1903",8,"high",NA,1900
-"52","latimes_18990204","""Los Angeles Times""",1899-02-04,15,NA,"""https://www.proquest.com/docview/163853622/590BBC08B3D34453PQ/70?accountid=14026""","“Among the fishermen outside yesterday in the choppy sea were two young men from San Diego, who had great sport catching a school of sea turtles into which their smack happened to run. The turtles were upon the surface of the sea, sunning themselves, and floating lazily along. The boys rigged up strong lines with nooses, and stole silently alongside the biggest fellow, who seemed to be asleep. With a quick jerk one of his flippers was caught, and the rope jerked taut. \n There was a lively sequel, and the big turtle pulled himself together and tried to dive. He could not, and reappearing, he started on a fast gait to the southward. The toys gradually hauled him to the gunwale, where with another line they got him into the boat. He weighed 276 pounds. In this manner they caught thirteen big turtles, running from eighty to 245 pounds. It is not often that the turtles are found off this part of the coast, as they prefer the warm water of the Gulf of California. \n The fish catch yesterday was: Halibut, 100; lobsters, 150 pounds, trout, 100, croakers, 175; silver smelt. 135 pounds.”","1","""FUN WITH SEA TURTLES.""","13","green","inferred","san_diego","inferred","276","not_reported","not_reported",NA,"1899",6,"medium",NA,1890
-"53","sdunion_19100905","""San Diego Union and Daily Bee""",1910-09-05,15,NA,"""https://cdnc.ucr.edu/?a=d&d=SDDU19100905.2.130&srpos=14&e=------191-en--20-SDDU-1--txt-txIN-turtle-------""","""Turtle Caught by Steve Zolezzie While He Was Fishing in Ocean South of San Diego. \n Ocean-Going Monster Weighing 487 Pounds Becomes Entangled in Net \n A giant green turtle which became entangled in nets of Steve Zolezzi, a local fisherman, was captured by him and a companion in the kelp near the boundary line yesterday morning. \n The big chelonian was found about 5 o'clock, when the fishermen went out to pay their usual morning visit to their nets. It had completely enmeshed itself and its captor worked hard for several hours before it was finally freed and the nets were hauled away from its vicious back-shaped jaws. One section of the nets was practically destroyed, involving a loss of about$50 to the owners. \n Despite the enormous size of the turtle it was finally dragged into Zolezzi’s boat by the fisherman and his companion and brought to San Diego. It was landed at the wharf of the San Diego fish market, where it was the cynosure of curious eyes during the entire day. It will not be killed until Monday, when, according to the statements of the market management last night, the edible portions of its huge hulk will be sold to Harry Rudder of the Union cafe. \n The turtle tipped the scales at 487 pounds.""","2","""GIANT TURTLE ENTRAPPED; SOON TO BE IN THE SOUP""","1","green","reported","san_diego","inferred","487","not_reported","""in the kelp near the boundary line""","""note that the name of the man who caught turtle is spelled two different ways (typo). While 487 lbs seems perhaps unrealistically heavy, it is an exact weight reported to be measured by scales, not an estimate.""","1910",9,"high",NA,1910
