+"85","slotribune_18840509","""San Luis Obispo Tribune""",1884-05-09,4,NA,"""https://cdnc.ucr.edu/?a=d&d=SLOTW18840509.2.18&srpos=9&e=-------en--20-SLOTW-1--txt-txIN-turtle+NOT+story+NOT+florida+NOT+jersey+NOT+bangor+NOT+cuba+NOT+jamaica+NOT+chicago+NOT+snapping+NOT+turn+NOT+turned+NOT+turns+NOT+turning+NOT+deck+NOT+dove+NOT+doves+NOT+house+NOT+pond+NOT+lake+NOT+York+NOT+desert+NOT+race+NOT+school+NOT+neck+NOT+mock+NOT+necks-------""","“While at Monterey on Friday last we saw a monster sea turtle that had been caught that day in the bay by some fishermen. The turtle appeared to be fully seven feet in length from nose to end of tail and with four long flippers, like wings, giving it a breadth of about the same. The monster was estimated to weigh 500 or 600 pounds. The captors expressed the intention of selling it for exhibition in Woodwards Garden in San Francisco.”","1","""Monster Turtle""","1","possible_leatherback","inferred","monterey_bay","known","600","7'","not_reported","""Inferred to be a leatherback based on size. This may potentially be the same event/observation as sbmp_18840509 based on location and time""","1884",7,"high",213.36,1,272.16,1880
+"86","sbmp_18840509","""Morning Press""",1884-05-09,3,NA,"""https://cdnc.ucr.edu/?a=d&d=MP18840509.2.12&srpos=33&e=-------en--20-MP-21--txt-txIN-turtle+NOT+story+NOT+florida+NOT+jersey+NOT+bangor+NOT+cuba+NOT+jamaica+NOT+chicago+NOT+snapping+NOT+turn+NOT+turned+NOT+turns+NOT+turning+NOT+deck+NOT+dove+NOT+doves+NOT+house+NOT+pond+NOT+lake+NOT+York+NOT+desert+NOT+race+NOT+school+NOT+neck+NOT+mock+NOT+necks-------""","“Friday while fishing in the bay on Monterey about five miles off shore, one of the boats of F. Nocefore & Co., saw a large turtle floating on the water. They succeeded in catching it with a gaff, and then securely tied it with ropes. Nine men tried to pull it into a boat, but were unable to move it. Three boats were required to tow it to Monterey. It is seven feet seven inches in length, four feet across the back, and has two fins three feet long. It is known as a humpback. —Santa Cruz Surf.”","2","""A Monster Turtle""","1","leatherback","inferred","monterey_bay","known","not_reported","7'7""","""floating on the water""","""The article refers to the species as a humpback—they likely are referring to it as a leatherback based on size. This may be the same event/observation (redundant) as slotribune_18840509 based on location and time. It also further specifies the size to be 4 feet in width and has 3 foot fins""","1884",9,"high",231.14,1,NA,1880
